    "problems": "The evaluated abstention is prompted by a safety-constrained instruction and concerns benign visual QA, not harmful requests. The paper reports no error bars, confidence intervals, or significance tests in the supplied text. The table shows some increases in incorrect outcomes after suppression, including Qwen3-VL on POPE.",
    "rows_left_out": "Figure-only layerwise visual-influence and refusal-projection trajectories, layer-specific intervention curves (Figures 2–5, 8–11), and qualitative examples (Tables 3–11) are not separately rowed; their plotted values are not stated numerically, and they do not test a claim version under the induced-behavior rule.",
